--> &ndash; <!--EndFragment-->2) = 0, such that <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = 2 or <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = <!--StartFragment-->&ndash;<!--EndFragment-->2. Therefore, <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = 2 is one solution to the original equation.</p><p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may be the result of computation errors.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":1,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959634,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"3de7a7d7","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1691007959634,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"08137-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"3bbc7575-e2d2-4579-b41a-0c420a9db765","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"08137-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is a solution to the equation <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x squared, minus 4, equals x squared\"></span></span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>1</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p>2</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p>3</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p>4</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. Subtracting <span class=\"italic\">x</span><sup>2</sup> from both sides of the given equation yields <span class=\"italic\">x</span><sup>2</sup> &ndash; 4 = 0. Adding 4 to both sides of the equation gives <span class=\"italic\">x</span><sup>2</sup> = 4. Taking the square root of both sides of the equation gives <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = 2 or <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = &ndash;2. Therefore, <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = 2 is one solution to the original equation.<p class=\"tcp-9d8041ce-388a-4d17-b627-3a24b2379e05\">Alternative approach: Subtracting <span class=\"italic\">x</span><sup>2</sup> from both sides of the given equation yields <span class=\"italic\">x</span><sup>2</sup> &ndash; 4 = 0. Factoring this equation gives <span class=\"italic\">x</span><sup>2</sup> &ndash; 4 = (<span class=\"italic\">x</span> + 2)(<span class=\"italic\">x</span><!--StartFragment--> &ndash; <!--EndFragment-->2) = 0, such that <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = 2 or <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = <!--StartFragment-->&ndash;<!--EndFragment-->2. Therefore, <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = 2 is one solution to the original equation.</p><p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may be the result of computation errors.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959634,"updateDate":1691007959634}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959634, 1691007959634),
    ($SATQ$3e28a622$SATQ$, $SATQ$f827079b-37e0-4696-9873-897b36b24545$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The function <math alttext="g"><mi>g</mi>
</math> is defined by&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals StartRoot x EndRoot plus 300"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>300</mn></mrow></math>. What is the value of&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> when&nbsp;<math alttext="x equals 81"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>81</mn></mrow></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"76cb5a6b-1d11-4ba2-8f01-15a6aedff96a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"48e9230e-9f78-448e-a647-e0e015fbafb1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"300\"><mn>300</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"285d88e2-2604-4dec-b7f7-c5355bf4529b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"309\"><mn>309</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3e6fe2f1-7951-46ff-a2dd-12285faa64a1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"381\"><mn>381</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["285d88e2-2604-4dec-b7f7-c5355bf4529b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct.&nbsp;It's given that function <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g"><mi>g</mi></math> is defined by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals StartRoot x EndRoot plus 300"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="81"><mn>81</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> in function <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g"><mi>g</mi></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis 81 right parenthesis equals StartRoot 81 EndRoot plus 300"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>81</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis 81 right parenthesis equals 9 plus 300"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis 81 right parenthesis equals 309"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>309</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 81"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="309"><mn>309</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 81 EndRoot"><msqrt><mn>81</mn></msqrt></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 81 EndRoot plus 300"><msqrt><mn>81</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></math>.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="81 plus 300"><mn>81</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 81 EndRoot plus 300"><msqrt><mn>81</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"3e28a622","external_id":"f827079b-37e0-4696-9873-897b36b24545","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"f6dfa166-8d60-444c-87f9-82ed7ce80360","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The function <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> is defined by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals StartRoot x EndRoot plus 300\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>300</mn></mrow></math>. What is the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> when&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x equals 81\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>81</mn></mrow></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"76cb5a6b-1d11-4ba2-8f01-15a6aedff96a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"48e9230e-9f78-448e-a647-e0e015fbafb1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"300\"><mn>300</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"285d88e2-2604-4dec-b7f7-c5355bf4529b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"309\"><mn>309</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3e6fe2f1-7951-46ff-a2dd-12285faa64a1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"381\"><mn>381</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["285d88e2-2604-4dec-b7f7-c5355bf4529b"],"correct_answer":["C"],"