    ($SATQ$42f8e4b4$SATQ$, $SATQ$44b4a3f1-1823-4c9d-984b-a4ea335c95ad$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$74b0fb54-95bb-4e47-894a-bfad018ce172$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Equivalent expressions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">One of the factors of <math alttext="2 x cubed plus 42 x squared plus 208 x"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>2</mn>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>3</mn>
		</msup>
	</mrow>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>42</mn>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
	</mrow>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>208</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> is <math alttext="x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mi>b</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>&nbsp;is a positive constant. What is the smallest possible value of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>. Since each term of the given expression, <math alttext="2 x cubed plus 42 x squared plus 208 x"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>42</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>208</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, has a factor of <math alttext="2 x"><mrow>
	<mn>2</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, the expression can be rewritten as <math alttext="2 x left parenthesis x squared right parenthesis plus 2 x left parenthesis 21 x right parenthesis plus 2 x left parenthesis 104 right parenthesis"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mn>104</mn></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="2 x left parenthesis x squared plus 21 x plus 104 right parenthesis"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>104</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Since the values <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math> have a sum of <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> and a product of <math alttext="104"><mn>104</mn>
</math>, the expression&nbsp;<math alttext="x squared plus 21 x plus 104"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>104</mn></math> can be factored as&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 8 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 13 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, the given expression can be factored as&nbsp;<math alttext="2 x left parenthesis x plus 8 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 13 right parenthesis"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. It follows that the factors of the given expression are <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="x plus 8"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>8</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, and <math alttext="x plus 13"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>13</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Of these factors, only <math alttext="x plus 8"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>8</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="x plus 13"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>13</mn>
</mrow>
</math> are of the form <math alttext="x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mi>b</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is a positive constant. Therefore, the possible values of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> are <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math>. Thus, the smallest possible value of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"42f8e4b4","external_id":"44b4a3f1-1823-4c9d-984b-a4ea335c95ad","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"74b0fb54-95bb-4e47-894a-bfad018ce172","uId":"b522620f-e882-4b76-8fca-da55631b072b","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">One of the factors of <math alttext=\"2 x cubed plus 42 x squared plus 208 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>42</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>208</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"x plus b\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>&nbsp;is a positive constant. What is the smallest possible value of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["8"],"correct_answer":["8"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math>. Since each term of the given expression, <math alttext=\"2 x cubed plus 42 x squared plus 208 x\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>42</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>208</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, has a factor of <math alttext=\"2 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the expression can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"2 x left parenthesis x squared right parenthesis plus 2 x left parenthesis 21 x right parenthesis plus 2 x left parenthesis 104 right parenthesis\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2<