<p style="text-align: left;">A conservation scientist implemented a program to reduce the population of a certain species in an area. The given function estimates this species' population <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> years after <math alttext="2008"><mn>2008</mn></math>, where <math alttext="x less than or equals 8"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Which of the following is the best interpretation of <math alttext="3,000"><mn>3,000</mn>
</math> in this context?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"25287970-1ce5-41a0-be4d-c2a528b7db8c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated percent decrease in the population for this species and area every <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> years after&nbsp;<math alttext=\"2008\"><mn>2008</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"e01df588-f925-47ea-b86d-d1bff711b17c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated percent decrease in the population for this species and area each year after <math alttext=\"2008\"><mn>2008</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"f703b13d-4c24-41b5-b8c4-25e4bbb2b8e6","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated population for this species and area <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;years after <math alttext=\"2008\"><mn>2008</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"35fff031-45d4-4a19-bab5-c20949684227","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The estimated initial population for this species and area in <math alttext=\"2008\"><mn>2008</mn></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["35fff031-45d4-4a19-bab5-c20949684227"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Substituting <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
