</math> years after <math alttext="2008"><mn>2008</mn></math>, so it follows that the estimated population of the species is <math alttext="3,000"><mn>3,000</mn>
</math> in <math alttext="2008"><mn>2008</mn></math>. Therefore, the best interpretation of <math alttext="3,000"><mn>3,000</mn>
</math> in this context is the estimated initial population for this species and area in <math alttext="2008"><mn>2008</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The estimated percent decrease in the population for this species and area each year after <math alttext="2008"><mn>2008</mn></math> is <math alttext="25 percent sign"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, not <math alttext="3,000"><mn>3,000</mn>
</math>.</p>
